            p[3] = 0;
         p += 4;
      }
   }
   return 1;
}
```

This function reads `p[0]`, `p[1]`, `p[2]` as bytes. For the 8-bit case, the output buffer has `out_n` bytes per pixel. For `out_n = 2`, it reads 1 byte and writes 1 byte. For `out_n = 4`, it reads 3 bytes and conditionally writes 1 byte.

